  "system": "You review Python code for object-level authorization (access control on a specific object).\nYou are given an access policy, the name of a target function, and some source code.\nDecide whether the target function, as written, lets a requester obtain or disclose an object's data in a way the policy forbids.\n\nRules:\n- Judge only from the code shown. Do not assume authorization logic that is not visible.\n- An `if` statement, or a name containing words such as \"owner\", \"check\", \"guard\" or \"auth\", is not evidence by itself. Confirm what is actually compared, with which values, and what happens when the comparison fails.\n- A call whose return value is ignored does not block anything unless the called code itself raises or stops execution.\n- Data that is returned, yielded, written, appended or sent before a failing check has already been disclosed.\n- If deciding requires code that is not shown (for example a called function whose body is missing), answer \"insufficient_context\" and name what is missing.\n- If the policy allows the access, it is not a problem.\n\nVerdict values:\n- \"vulnerable\": the visible code lets a requester access or disclose data against the policy.\n- \"no_issue_found\": the visible code enforces the policy for the target function.\n- \"insufficient_context\": the decision depends on code that is not shown.\n\nReply with JSON only: {\"verdict\": ..., \"evidence\": ..., \"missing_context\": [...]}.\n\"evidence\" quotes the relevant code lines and explains them briefly. \"missing_context\" lists the missing information (empty list if none).",
  "prompt": "ACCESS POLICY:\nA user may change only their own email address.\n\nENDPOINT: PUT /users/v1/{username}/email\nTARGET FUNCTION: api_views.users.update_email (the handler of this endpoint)\n\nCODE:\n```python\n# file: api_views/users.py\ndef update_email(username):\n    request_data = request.get_json()\n    try:\n        jsonschema.validate(request_data, update_email_schema)\n    except:\n        return Response(error_message_helper('Please provide a proper JSON body.'), 400, mimetype='application/json')\n    resp = token_validator(request.headers.get('Authorization'))\n    if 'error' in resp:\n        return Response(error_message_helper(resp), 401, mimetype='application/json')\n    else:\n        user = User.query.filter_by(username=resp['sub']).first()\n        regex = '^[a-z0-9]+[\\\\._]?[a-z0-9]+[@]\\\\w+[.]\\\\w{2,3}$'\n        if re.search(regex, request_data.get('email')):\n            user.email = request_data.get('email')\n            db.session.commit()\n            responseObject = {'status': 'success', 'data': {'username': user.username, 'email': user.email}}\n            return Response(json.dumps(responseObject), 204, mimetype='application/json')\n        else:\n            return Response(error_message_helper('Please Provide a valid email address.'), 400, mimetype='application/json')\n```\n\nCONTEXT NOTE:\nOnly selected functions from the codebase are shown. Classes (including data models and schemas) and module-level variables are not shown.\nCalls not shown:\n- api_views.users.error_message_helper(...): defined in this codebase but not shown (call depth limit)\n- api_views.users.token_validator(...): defined in this codebase but not shown (call depth limit)\n- request.get_json(...) called in api_views.users.update_email: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- jsonschema.validate(...) called in api_views.users.update_email: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- Response(...) called in